<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The Halo 3-style multiplayer pause screen (Menu style Halo 3), built into each level's map
with the campaign's (ingame.txt): it stands for the Xbox's multiplayer pause screen of a player
alone on their machine (ui\shell\multiplayer_game\pause_game\1p_pause_game, which Start opens in
a multiplayer game: ui_widget.c ui_check_for_pause_game; split screen's 2p and 4p screens, each
player's own over their part of the screen, stay the Xbox's) and does what that one does - RESUME
and its quit, the Xbox's own "mp game player quit" - laid out as pause.xml (its fonts and
pictures, the same set): the game type and map in the title strip, the score to win under it,
the column of choices at the left, the game's panel at the right, the buttons in a strip at the
bottom. As the Xbox's, it never pauses the game (no pause_game flag). Its rows
(menu_functions.c "port h3 mp pause ..."):
- RESUME;
- PLAYERS: Halo 3's roster (players.xml: add friend, block);
- SETTINGS: the profile's controls, as CUSTOMIZATION's (stick and button layout, look sensitivity,
  invert look and flight, auto-center, vibration: the Xbox profile's fields, saved to it on Circle
  and played at once), and ALL SETTINGS, the settings panel. The Xbox's multiplayer pause has no
  settings of its own (Halo PC's had, and its maps' are taken out: cache_file_formats.c
  multiplayer_pause_list_convert);
- PARTY, in a party only: the settings panel's Party page (its chat and quick chat);
- LEAVE GAME for a machine that joined, END GAME for the host's: Halo 3's question first, then the
  Xbox's quit (the same function its pause ran, for every network: system link, online, a
  dedicated server's or a PC's game).
No CHANGE TEAMS: the Xbox changes a player's team in the game's lobby only (its server refuses a
player's settings once the game has started: network_server_message_handler.c). In a Forge game
the Forge menu opens instead (forge.xml), as before. The art is this folder's own
(tools/halo3_menu_art.py). -->
<menus root="h3/mppause/screen" replaces="ui\shell\multiplayer_game\pause_game\1p_pause_game">
